<section class="chapter" id="overview">
  <div class="panel panel--cool">
    <div class="chapter__inner">
      <h2 class="section-title">4. System Overview</h2>

      <p>Listening A[i]gent has four core capability areas:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Capture</strong> — collect signals from existing artifacts (notes, comments, scorecards, retros).</li>
        <li><strong>Structure</strong> — normalize into a taxonomy (theme, risk, severity, confidence, owner).</li>
        <li><strong>Triage</strong> — route to the right owner with suggested next steps.</li>
        <li><strong>Close the loop</strong> — track actions and communicate “what changed.”</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4.1 Inputs (Examples)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Interview feedback + scorecard comments</li>
        <li>Recruiter / HRBP notes</li>
        <li>Manager 1:1 summaries</li>
        <li>Exit and transition summaries</li>
        <li>Operational retrospectives</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>4.2 Outputs</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Thematic summaries tied to specific workflows</li>
        <li>Early-warning indicators (friction, burnout, confusion)</li>
        <li>Decision-ready insight for Ops and leadership</li>
        <li>Documented feedback loops showing “what changed”</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" id="taxonomy">
  <div class="panel panel--cool">
    <div class="chapter__inner">
      <h2 class="section-title">5. Signal Taxonomy</h2>

      <p>Signals should be structured consistently so teams can compare apples to apples.</p>

      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Field</th>
              <th>Description</th>
              <th>Example Values</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>theme</code></td>
              <td>High-level topic area</td>
              <td>Role clarity, workload, tools, manager quality, process friction</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>signal_type</code></td>
              <td>What kind of feedback this is</td>
              <td>Friction, risk, suggestion, praise, confusion, policy gap</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>severity</code></td>
              <td>Potential impact if true</td>
              <td>Low / Medium / High</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>confidence</code></td>
              <td>How certain we are</td>
              <td>Low / Medium / High (based on corroboration)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>source</code></td>
              <td>Where it came from</td>
              <td>1:1 note, interview feedback, retro doc, exit summary</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>attribution</code></td>
              <td>How identity is handled</td>
              <td>Named / role-level / anonymized</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>owner</code></td>
              <td>Who must respond</td>
              <td>HRBP, manager, Ops, IT, leadership</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>status</code></td>
              <td>Closed-loop stage</td>
              <td>Captured → Triaged → In progress → Resolved → Communicated</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Rule:</strong> A signal without an owner is just noise.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" id="workflows">
  <div class="panel panel--cool">
    <div class="chapter__inner">
      <h2 class="section-title">6. Capture &amp; Workflow Patterns</h2>

      <h3>6.1 Lightweight Capture (Best Default)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Add a simple “Signal tags” section to existing docs/templates (retro notes, 1:1 prompts).</li>
        <li>Allow quick tagging: theme + severity + suggested owner.</li>
        <li>Weekly triage by People Ops/HRBP.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>6.2 Structured Capture Points</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>ID</th>
              <th>Capture Point</th>
              <th>Trigger</th>
              <th>Output</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>L1</td>
              <td>Exit / transition summary</td>
              <td>Exit initiated</td>
              <td>Top 3 themes + actionable owners</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>L2</td>
              <td>Manager 1:1 summary</td>
              <td>Weekly/biweekly cadence</td>
              <td>Friction + risk flags for triage</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>L3</td>
              <td>Retro notes</td>
              <td>Project milestone</td>
              <td>Process / tooling issues with timestamps</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>L4</td>
              <td>Interview feedback (candidate experience)</td>
              <td>Interview completed</td>
              <td>CX friction themes + ownership</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3>6.3 Triage Loop</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Weekly:</strong> HRBP/Ops reviews new signals and assigns owners.</li>
        <li><strong>Biweekly:</strong> validate repeat signals (raise confidence if corroborated).</li>
        <li><strong>Monthly:</strong> leadership summary of top themes + actions shipped.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" id="implementation">
  <div class="panel panel--cool">
    <div class="chapter__inner">
      <h2 class="section-title">7. Implementation Notes</h2>

      <h3>7.1 Where It Lives</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Docs-first:</strong> simplest — tags inside existing notes and templates.</li>
        <li><strong>System-first:</strong> structured form fields in HRIS/ATS (where appropriate).</li>
        <li><strong>Hybrid:</strong> tags in docs + periodic structured rollup.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>7.2 Access &amp; Retention</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Define a retention policy for raw notes vs. aggregated insights.</li>
        <li>Restrict access to named attribution; share trends at aggregate level.</li>
        <li>Log who viewed or exported sensitive summaries.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>Default recommendation:</strong> Start docs-first for 30–45 days, prove value, then add structure.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" id="metrics">
  <div class="panel panel--cool">
    <div class="chapter__inner">
      <h2 class="section-title">8. Metrics &amp; Reporting</h2>

      <p>Measure whether listening becomes action:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Time from signal captured → owner assigned</li>
        <li>Time from owner assigned → action shipped</li>
        <li>% of signals with closed-loop communication</li>
        <li>Repeat-signal rate by theme (is the system improving?)</li>
        <li>Top friction themes by org / role family (with thresholds)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>8.1 Integration with Metrics A[i]gent</h3>
      <p>
        Listening signals can be mapped to a shared metrics layer as event objects:
        <code>signal_captured</code>, <code>signal_triaged</code>, <code>action_shipped</code>, <code>loop_closed</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="chapter" id="suite">
  <div class="panel panel--cool">
